id: pm-rust-cbaq
title: Extend native list selection to configured lifecycle and hierarchy registries
description: "Follow-up to the built-in list pagination slice. Native selection currently uses canonical lifecycle and parent/child relationship kinds. Add configured status buckets, terminal classification and custom hierarchy kinds using real disposable-tracker differentials against the pinned oracle. Preserve page fingerprints and full JSON/TOON envelopes."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[3]: follow-up,read-parity,rust
created_at: "2026-10-15T11:08:01.726Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T01:55:27.381Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Configured status and hierarchy definitions produce identical selected rows, sorting, fingerprints and multi-page JSON/TOON envelopes to the pinned oracle; preserve all four 100 percent coverage dimensions"
parent: pm-rust-ufzy
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T11:26:11.524Z",codex-agent,Created after duplicate search during pm-rust-ufzy. The delivered pagination slice targets built-in lifecycle and hierarchy registries. This child retains configured-registry selection and cursor conformance as separate follow-up work; no implementation or closure claim.
  "2026-10-15T21:41:38.639Z",codex-agent,"Implement configured lifecycle buckets, terminal ordering and dependency hierarchy selection. Verify byte-exact JSON and TOON pages and continuations with disposable trackers against the locked oracle; record isolated behavioural revert proofs and full release gates."
  "2026-10-15T21:47:35.582Z",codex-agent,"The locked oracle resolves custom hierarchy kinds through extension registration, with no persisted definition format. Native selection reads a declarative schema.relationship_kinds snapshot using the oracle definition fields (kind, aliases, hierarchy, hierarchyDirection). Disposable oracle trackers activate a real schema extension registering those same definitions. No JavaScript is executed by native production code; arbitrary extension activation remains outside this slice."
  "2026-10-15T21:55:00.100Z",codex-agent,"Configured hierarchy fixtures now include dependency created_at provenance after the pinned oracle rejected multi-row dependencies without timestamps. The independent oracle read gap is tracked in pm-rust-tdps. Custom status fingerprints also retain projectionCommand=list, excludeTerminal and the raw status semantic option, matching the oracle rather than inventing a list-custom-status command."
  "2026-10-15T21:58:32.854Z",codex-agent,"Five isolated behavioural negative controls each rebuilt and ran cargo test --locked --test pagination_differential configured_registry_selection_regressions -- --exact --nocapture, failing on wire stdout with Cargo exit 101: restore exact-status-only Lifecycle::matches; restore built-in-only Lifecycle::terminal; restore built-in-only Hierarchy::source_parent; revert only cursor_fingerprint to the base implementation; restore only the built-in dependency_blocked_ids body. Every mutation was restored in finally before the next control. Oracle fixtures, launcher and expectations stayed unchanged."
  "2026-10-15T22:06:16.700Z",codex-agent,"First-read parity finding: the pinned oracle creates built-in schema scaffold files when absent; their workflows then override inline schema.workflow values. Native list models those missing-file defaults in memory and remains read-only. Custom fixture configurations now persist their status/workflow schema files before either CLI reads them, with nonempty bucket assertions. A separate first-read differential removes only the disposable schema directory, compares JSON and TOON, and proves native list creates no schema files."
  "2026-10-15T22:13:51.684Z",codex-agent,"Final source verification: all seven behavioural negative controls were refreshed against the original main implementations and failed on their intended assertions (Cargo exit 101), then restored. Registry edge contracts passed 4/4. The complete configured differential passed 4/4 before splitting its three independent lifecycle configurations into separate concurrent tests to bound CI duration; no fixture or selection semantics changed in that split."
  "2026-10-15T22:21:27.737Z",codex-agent,"Final focused receipts: pm test --run --timeout 600 --progress passed all 6 configured lifecycle/hierarchy/scaffold tests; the additional empty-active-role actionability differential passed 1/1 through pm test --only-last. Registry edge contracts pass 5/5. An eighth isolated behavioural revert replaces only active_for_blocking with active-role membership; configured_no_active_role_blockers_match_oracle then fails on wire stdout with Cargo exit 101. The mutation was restored. All 8 negative controls fail behaviourally, not at compile time."
  "2026-10-15T23:08:42.326Z",codex-agent,"The first complete release aggregate executed 338 ordinary and 338 instrumented tests across 18 targets each, zero failures or ignored tests, but correctly failed the unchanged coverage floor: lines 6416/6416, functions 612/612 and branches 1378/1378 were complete; regions were 9979/9982. The three missed regions were I/O error propagation. Lifecycle now captures hierarchy from the same settings read, removing the duplicate read and its race-only error path. A real directory-as-workflow-file test exercises workflow and list error propagation. Targeted instrumented units pass 5/5 and cover all 297 registry regions; all 8 behavioural revert controls were refreshed successfully and restored. Rerunning the complete aggregate on the consolidated implementation."
  "2026-10-15T23:57:19.714Z",codex-agent,"Complete release-check passed on source head 5e00a16 with clean HOME and neutral global Git configuration. Ordinary and instrumented suites each pass 338 tests across 18 targets, zero failed or ignored. Coverage meets every unchanged 100 percent floor: lines 6412/6412, functions 611/611, regions 9972/9972, branches 1378/1378. Formatting, deny-warning Clippy, private-item rustdoc, identity audit 7/7, cargo audit over 134 dependencies (no vulnerabilities; one existing allowed unmaintained advisory), and changelog check pass. All 8 independent behavioural revert controls fail on intended assertions and are restored. Native custom hierarchy uses the documented declarative snapshot of the active oracle extension registry. Releasing ownership, retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-15T23:58:32.338Z",codex-agent,"Final oracle tracker-health gate passes 8/8 checks with clone-local merge drivers required and strict exit enabled, using a clean HOME and neutral Git configuration. Three existing guidance, staleness and provenance advisories remain advisory. Both implementation claims are released; cbaq and oqst stay in_progress for orchestrator verification, and the independent oracle-read follow-up pm-rust-tdps stays open."
  "2026-10-16T00:14:41.229Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: inspected CI run 38826941351. macOS and Windows both fail only workflow_fallbacks_and_settings_errors at the exact workflow-directory I/O path assertion. Main is already an ancestor of this branch. Registry reads use canonical pm_root; query spelling is physical on Unix and caller-resolved on Windows. Align registry reads and exact-path tests with that established platform contract; audit all new PR path assertions and rerun the full aggregate plus platform CI."
  "2026-10-16T00:15:29.016Z",codex-agent,"Path assertion audit: the workflow-directory assertion is the only new raw filesystem-path equality in this PR. It now independently derives absolute input spelling on Windows and canonical physical spelling on Unix, matching the workspace tests, and still requires typed Io for that exact workflow path. A test-first CI checkpoint will retain the old list registry call to prove the Windows production defect before restoring the corrected function. No arbitrary-Io relaxation."
  "2026-10-16T00:15:56.408Z",codex-agent,"Unix spelling negative control: cargo test --locked --lib list_registry::tests::workflow_fallbacks_and_settings_errors -- --exact was rebuilt with only the original test function restored and a symlink-spelled temporary root. It failed at the original path equality (0 passed, 1 failed, exit 101). Restoring the platform-aware assertion under the same symlink root passed 1/1. This reproduces the macOS physical-root mismatch on Linux without changing production or weakening error identity. Windows function-revert proof will use the unchanged production list function in the test-first CI checkpoint."
  "2026-10-16T00:16:58.725Z",codex-agent,"Production decision: list registry settings/schema reads now use Workspace::query_pm_root(), as query fingerprints already do. Unix retains physical roots; Windows retains resolved input aliases rather than canonical verbatim/expanded spelling. The exact expected error root is derived independently in the test using absolute() on Windows and canonicalize() on Unix. The test-first checkpoint is 61939c7; its old production call is the Windows behavioral negative control. Running the repository-native just release-check (there is no root package.json) with clean HOME and neutral Git configuration at unchanged coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-16T00:20:20.651Z",codex-agent,"Windows behavioral function-revert proof: test-first head 61939c7 contains the final exact-path regression test but retains the original list function calling Lifecycle::load(workspace.pm_root()). CI run 38828544829, Rust windows-latest job 116741804433, fails only workflow_fallbacks_and_settings_errors: 161 passed, 1 failed, exit 101. The assertion shows canonical verbatim-prefix and expanded-name output versus resolved 8.3-alias input spelling. This differs from the final implementation by only the registry-root argument in the production list function; restoring query_pm_root() is the fix. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/38828544829/job/116741804433 ."
  "2026-10-16T01:07:39.491Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 complete local gate receipt on source commit a6bac79: just release-check passed with clean HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1, using the locked published oracle. The Rust-only repository has no root npm/bun release:check script; just release-check is its documented aggregate. Ordinary and instrumented suites each passed 338 tests across 18 targets, zero failed or ignored. Unchanged coverage floors all pass: lines 6412/6412, functions 611/611, regions 9972/9972, branches 1378/1378. Formatting, deny-warning Clippy, private-item rustdoc, identity audit 7/7, cargo audit over 134 dependencies and changelog check pass; the existing allowed unsafe-libyaml unmaintained warning remains. Strict tracker health with required clone-local merge drivers also passes 8/8 using clean HOME and neutral Git configuration, with three existing advisories. The linked focused test was run through pm test --run --only-last --progress and passed 1/1. Unix and Windows negative controls are documented above. Pushing the corrected implementation next; final platform CI remains required."
  "2026-10-16T01:29:16.615Z",codex-agent,"Corrected-head CI run 38833447003: all three Rust jobs pass, including the exact workflow error regression on Windows (162/162 library tests). macOS and Ubuntu release aggregates and CodeQL pass. Windows release aggregate job 116757156990 hit its 20-minute job deadline after both full test passes succeeded and coverage passed at lines 6413/6413, functions 611/611, regions 9983/9983, branches 1382/1382; cancellation occurred as cargo audit began. This is missing aggregate evidence, not a pass. Increase only the Windows aggregate time budget to 30 minutes so audit, changelog and strict health can finish; preserve every command and threshold. Rust source remains a6bac79 and retains the complete clean-HOME local gate receipt. Validate the workflow change with the existing release-pipeline contract suite, then push and require a complete new CI run."
  "2026-10-16T01:30:40.226Z",codex-agent,"Workflow budget validation passes: cargo test --locked --test release_pipeline_contract ran through pm test --run --only-last --progress with 18 passed, zero failed or ignored. The existing contract suite parses both workflows and verifies gate/toolchain/history requirements. GitHub context availability permits matrix in jobs timeout-minutes, so the expression selects 30 minutes only for Windows and retains 20 for the other aggregate runners. Every release-check command and 100 percent threshold is unchanged. Rust production source remains identical to the locally certified a6bac79 tree; only the Windows aggregate job budget and tracker evidence changed after that complete local gate."
  "2026-10-16T01:55:23.882Z",codex-agent,"Complete corrected-platform CI receipt: head 08f34c1523553dd3d8bf1bb07aeeb160000f3f63, CI run 38835538531, all six jobs success: Rust ubuntu-latest, Rust macos-latest, Rust windows-latest, Release gate aggregate, Release gate aggregate macos-latest, Release gate aggregate windows-latest. CodeQL and Analyze Rust also pass. Windows aggregate completed in 21m22s, beyond the previous 20-minute deadline: 330 ordinary and 330 instrumented tests across 18 targets each, zero failed or ignored, all four unchanged coverage floors at 100 percent, followed by successful audit, changelog and strict tracker health. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/38835538531 . The previously failing exact workflow-path test passes on both platforms; behavioral negative controls and local Linux 338/338 receipts are recorded above. The final tracker-receipt commit changes no Rust source or workflow behavior and will receive another complete CI verification before delivery. Automated review services were skipped; no review approval claim. No new pm CLI/SDK bug found. Releasing ownership and retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification."
